 {
  "verse_id": "tsa-a15-v07",
  "song": "tsa-a15",
  "verse": 7,
  "quick_english": "But if he shows a with-conviction, seedless initiation to a fool and to one whose power-descent has come — then at Śiva-hand-giving-time this rite: contemplating in the right hand a triangular, āgneya, flame-terrible, repha-spark, outward-vāta-wheel-rolling mandala, casting a little seed therein in the hand itself, by the up-down repha-revealed phaṭkāra successions he burns her generative-power. Doing thus, he casts that hand onto the disciple's head. Thus for both this seedless initiation destroys the capacity for doing one's own work — because even inanimate things are stated as initiatable. Let him contemplate the disciple installed inside the vāyupura, shaken, become-light — by which, by comparison, he is seen as light.",
